# SS-19 - ELI15-first DeepSeaFoam learning experience
Workstream ID: SS-19
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/19
Status: DONE
Milestone: M1.1
Dependencies: SS-01, SS-04, SS-05

## Purpose
Make the entire tool understandable without prior stock-market knowledge, while
keeping exact rules, real observations and a clean, compact DeepSeaFoam interface.

## Tasks
- [x] Research canonical color roles, native charts and controllable motion.
- [x] Add an original vector logo, tonal cards and focused chart views.
- [x] Write seven plain-English pattern lessons with buy/sell rules and failure explanations.
- [x] Add a pattern explanation button, hover definitions and a searchable dictionary.
- [x] Give every authored explanation a vegetables/toys/household analogy; audit visible vocabulary.
- [x] Verify replay safety, explanatory navigation, optional motion and compact layouts.
- [x] Capture actual-data GUI screenshots and make the README image-led and ELI15-first.
- [x] Synchronize the issue/Project, record evidence and update owned continuity.
- [x] Show the supplied Stonks GIF during stock downloads, with optional motion and completion cleanup.
- [x] Replace the shared logo with a sniper reticle aimed at a candlestick chart.
- [x] Apply square corners consistently to rectangular GUI surfaces and controls.
- [x] Replace the logo tile with erratic rectangular-chart search, centered lock,
  a visible bullet and a transparent circular finish; center the still reticle.
  Share the animation between the app header and four-times-larger README logo.
- [x] Make README gold/green and GIF-led, with image navigation buttons and
  linked setup/explanation guides.
- [x] Match the square chart's outer side to the final circle's outer diameter.

## Acceptance criteria
- No market knowledge is assumed: basics such as a share, price, exchange and cash have explanations.
- Technical words are explained before use or have discoverable hover/click help.
- Pattern and dictionary explanations include relatable everyday examples, clearly separated from actual market observations.
- Hover help has an equivalent clickable/keyboard-accessible dictionary route.
- A selected pattern has a direct explanation button and exact sourced rules remain accessible.
- Search accepts common names and abbreviations and explicitly reports no match.
- Charts/results remain causal; changing the drawn window never changes the test.
- Motion can be disabled; no automatic playback or constant animation is required.
- Downloads show the requested stock and supplied GIF without artificial delays;
  success and failure both restore the workspace. Disabled motion keeps the GIF still.
- The main desktop workspace has no page scrollbar at representative desktop sizes.
- The shared app/README logo clearly shows a circular scope and crosshairs over price candles.
- Rectangular cards, controls, list selections, chart backgrounds and logo tile
  have square corners; the later logo follow-up removes its tile entirely.
- Animated branding searches the rectangular chart, settles centrally, fires a
  visible bullet and cuts to a circle with transparent surroundings. The matching
  still reticle is centered, including when header motion is disabled.
  The 352px README logo is 4x its original 88px width.
- The search chart is square, with exactly the final circle's visible width and
  height, including borders; the cut changes shape without changing size.
- README uses gold/green linked image buttons and native GIF demos with honest
  data provenance; longer explanations remain accessible in linked guides.
- Screenshots show the real native application with actual observations, not a fictional dashboard.
- Technical checks, human comprehension testing and normal Windows/DPI qualification are recorded separately.

## Completion evidence
- Seven plain-language lessons and 74 shared dictionary entries pair meanings with
  everyday examples. Search covers names/abbreviations and explicitly reports gaps.
- Real widget hover and Tab/Return navigation open the shared explanations without
  changing the experiment. All seven rule-guide charts pass prefix-safety checks.
- 47 tests, Ruff lint/format and strict source mypy passed. Drawing-window tests
  preserve calculations/running highs; motion-off stops playback and transitions.
- Six inspected native screenshots use actual RELIANCE.NS observations, at
  1440x900 and 1366x768. The main workspace fits without a page scrollbar;
  long explanation panels can scroll. README embeds each view with a caption.
- Live checks ran all seven rules on RELIANCE.NS=494, TCS.NS=494 and TCS.BO=492
  completed daily observations. docs/images/captures.json records gallery provenance.
- Explicit native chart ownership, deferred chart cleanup, SVG rendering and
  button styling fixes are recorded in docs/development.md.
- Human comprehension, normal Windows/DPI and installer acceptance remain unverified.
  Actual provider retrieval is not independent market-price reconciliation.
- Loading follow-up: six desktop and ten learning tests passed, with Ruff lint/format
  and strict source mypy. Tests verify actual frame advancement, paused motion,
  mid-download toggles, worker success/failure and stopped hidden animation.
- A separate installed candidate wheel contains the exact supplied 30-frame,
  infinitely looping GIF. Its loading view was inspected at 1366x768 with an owned,
  blocked test provider; no market observations were generated or claimed.
  The published v0.1.0 wheel remains unchanged.
- Logo follow-up: the shared SVG has a seafoam scope, pale reticle and five
  green/red candles. Native Qt icon rendering was inspected at 42, 88 and 256px.
- Square-corner follow-up: 16 desktop/learning tests, Ruff lint/format and strict
  source mypy passed. Inspected all four tabs and the loading surface in an owned
  1366x768 native window; all four chart backgrounds have zero roundness.
  No network retrieval, market observations or existing-user-window control.
- Animated presentation follow-up: 50 tests, Ruff lint/format and strict source
  mypy passed. Actual header-frame movement, transparent corners, pause/resume
  and close cleanup are covered. Separate installed-wheel smoke confirmed
  exact SVG/GIF assets and runtime motion without changing the existing release.
- Inspected original circular search/lock/flash frames, 46/88/256px native still
  icons, gold/green banner/buttons and five native 1366x768 GIF demos.
  The demos use 493 actual RELIANCE.NS observations through 2026-11-09;
  docs/images/gif-captures.json records the explicit historical cutoff.
  A latest-range request failed price validation; no invented fallback was used.
- Revised animation: inspected erratic rectangular-chart search, centered lock,
  visible bullet/tracer, impact and circular cut. All 70 frames decode in Qt;
  final outside pixels are transparent. Native still reticle is centered.
  Explicit painter clips correct Qt's ignored SVG clip path.
  Final 51 tests, Ruff lint/format and strict source mypy passed. Motion-off
  shows the centered still; resume restores animation. A separately installed
  candidate verified exact packaged assets, clipping and motion/close behavior.
- Equal-size follow-up: every frame retains 328x328px visible bounds. The square's
  outer side equals the circle's outer diameter, including their borders.
  Inspected first/final frames together; eight desktop tests and targeted Ruff
  lint/format passed. The regression failed against the old 332x244px stage.
  No market retrieval, gallery recapture or published-package replacement.

